From: GZ302 camera bring-up <local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: recognize the GZ302 OV13B10 ISP sensor

The ASUS ROG Flow Z13 GZ302EA exposes its rear OmniVision OV13B10 sensor as
ACPI HID OMNI13B1.  AMDGPU currently recognizes only the reference OMNI5C10
sensor for ISP4 setup, so it declines to create the ISP capture, I2C and GPIO
MFD devices on this laptop.

Add the GZ302 sensor HID to AMDGPU's ISP allow-list.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_acpi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_acpi.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_acpi.c
@@ -1588,6 +1588,7 @@
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DRM_AMD_ISP)
 static const struct acpi_device_id isp_sensor_ids[] = {
 	{ "OMNI5C10" },
+	{ "OMNI13B1" }, /* ASUS ROG Flow Z13 (GZ302EA), OV13B10 rear camera */
 	{ }
 };
 
